all right southwest medical is wishing  you all a happy  healthy new year here's how they can  help you stay well in 2021  so let's start talking about how people  can you know  bring in this new year their healthiest  selves  yes absolutely you know especially in  light of the year that we've just  finished our hope is to make sure that  all of our patients in all of our  communities make this the best year yet  and really with paying attention to  their preventative health care  definitely and you know is it safe to go  into the doctor's office because  obviously that was a huge  question on people's minds in 2020 but  it's trickling into 2021 as well  most definitely you know it's important  to point out that even before the  pandemic  doctor's offices were a safe place there  were a lot of protocols and provisions  that were made  and after the pandemic there's so much  that has changed  to increase and heighten our levels of  sanitation as well as protection  of all medical staff as well as all of  our patients  including limiting the number of  visitors in our buildings screening  anyone and everyone who comes to those  buildings mandating masks and  encouraging hand hygiene as well and  what's the best way to  start a healthy new year  that's a great question and i'm so glad  to bring that up because when it's the  start of a new year we're always trying  to think of  what can we do to keep ourselves healthy  make ourselves healthier  and the answer that really lies in  prevention paying attention to  preventative health  meaning paying attention to things  before we start to  look or feel unwell is so important and  that's really the background behind  primary care medicine  so i encourage all patients to connect  with their primary care providers  and discuss their preventative health  care and then next you just have your  annual wellness visit right and that's  how you can continue to keep track of  where you are most definitely the annual  wellness  visit allows you a one-on-one time with  your provider  to discuss all of your health concerns  and questions  but also to look at specific risk  factors and screening that are tailored  to you  your age your race your history and  certainly things that may be found on  your physical exam  tailored to your specific needs to keep  you as healthy as possible  so in addition to the history that we  take there's a lot of different tests  that can be done in the office  things like ekg tests bone density tests  tests that screen for your mental health  or cognitive impairment  as well as things like circulation nerve  conduction  and diabetes now are there people that  are more at risk if they do not stay on  top of their health care routines  absolutely well prevention is there for  everybody it is important to recognize  that our patients 65  and older might be at higher risk  especially those patients who might have  chronic conditions  such as diabetes as an example 34  million people in the united states have  diabetes  there's other chronic conditions such as  heart disease cancer  and lung disease and it's estimated from  the cdc that six out of  every ten adults in the united states  have at least one chronic care condition  and at least four out of ten have two or  more that's a lot of people that we're  talking about and it's so important for  those individuals to stay up to date  on their chronic care as well as for  their preventative care  and that's also why health screenings  exist right  absolutely screenings are there to help  us look for things  before they have a chance to make us  look or feel  unwell southwest medical has locations  across southern nevada call that number  right there on your screen or just visit  smalv.com for more information
 

